  "verbalization": "Trigonostemonine C appears to be a potential inhibitor of ME-180 through a series of molecular interactions involving the CD276 antigen. The evidence suggests that Trigonostemonine C targets the CD276 antigen, which is then recognized by 1-Hydroxy-7-methoxyxanthone, Patchoulane, or 2,2,4-Trimethyl-3-cyclohexenecarboxaldehyde, all of which ultimately have ME-180 as their target. These pathways are interconnected, indicating a possible hierarchical mechanism where Trigonostemonine C may modulate the expression or activity of CD276, thereby influencing ME-180's function. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and reliable relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Trigonostemonine C affects ME-180 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise role of Trigonostemonine C in the regulation of ME-180.",
